#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292940 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ccc7f71-d2e0-5f35-80a5-042a53eda2da" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Equation of a Parabola Given Its Parametric Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f803e75-9b26-5e64-a1d6-7b797e1d6f4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f803e75-9b26-5e64-a1d6-7b797e1d6f4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292942} :answer-field/id #uuid "e99c9df6-f2cc-5ed9-a171-8462a5376590" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0fe4c9ac-c3be-5ca2-8785-0a4e82bd680c" :question/math-academy-id "q-280361" :question/problem "Consider the following parabola:\n\n$$\nx=-2t,\\,y=-\\frac{4}{3}{t}^{2},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of the parabola is\n\n${x}^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =-\\frac{x}{2},\\,{t}^{2}=-\\frac{3y}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-\\frac{3y}{4}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =-\\frac{3y}{4} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-3y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian equation of the parabola is ${x}^{2}=-3y.$"}]}
